sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-collective-03> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The number of individuals formed by an embryonic blastoderm is not fixed at one by the genome: temporarily introducing breaks that informationally isolate islands of cells yields twins, triplets and so on, showing the blastoderm is an excitable medium in which several coherent embryos can self-organize.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The number of embryos a blastoderm forms is not fixed by genetics";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "McMillen P, Levin M, “Collective intelligence: A unifying concept for integrating biology across scales and substrates”, Communications biology (2024), doi:10.1038/s42003-024-06037-4; section “Introduction › Development: transition to multicellularity”. Scope: Early vertebrate (e.g. avian) blastoderms"
}
